ge image borders running off the  page calls a sense of unease to the  reader and not in a good way for  instance if you are looking at a picture  online you probably position it such  that you can see all of the image on the  screen typically you don't leave the  image on the border are slightly under  because there is a nagging sensation in  our brains telling us to scroll down  because we might not have all of the  image visible so when Toyo taro leaves  this image run off the bottom of the  page the readers are given a feeling  that they want to scroll down or reveal  more of the image in other words there's  a sense that they aren't seeing the full  picture from a psychological standpoint  this makes sense and when we compare it  with Toriyama's box approach everything  looks tidier and easier to read as a  result another added benefit to this  practice is that it allows the artist to  think outside the box from time to time  for example take a look at what I did  with the same scene keeping the panel  boxes closed on the bottom and top I was  able to break those rules specifically  with the character's anatomy to create  the illusion they are reaching outside  of their box this adds energy to a scene  catch the reader's eye and helps your  image leap off the page now that we've  covered the visual noise and the visual  itch two aspects I don't think get  nearly enough attention I think it's  time to discuss the part of Toyota ROS  game that gets it the most flack I am  speaking about the visual stench what I  mean by visual stage is the  that comes over you when you were  reading through Toyota Rose manga this  feeling tells you there's something  fishy about this and in many aspects  you'd be right  I'm sure many of you have seen this if  you go around Twitter the same time the  manga chapters are released each month  propagating the web are scandalous  images showing the world Toyota Rose  proclivities when it comes to drawing  and the bad habits he has as an artist  people complain fervently about his lack  of knowledge when it comes to Anatomy  and yeah I can see why that might be an  issue for some but for me the visual  standing comes from his seeming  inability to avoid using the same poses  over and over and over again  one of his lesser-known repeating  offences are the boring flat side  profile combat shots in this chapter  alone there are four panels that have  this boring composition that angle is  not good it shows no depth and it's like  something a four-year-old would compose  if he was gifted the abilities to know  taro has it requires no creativity and  no imagination I hate using this word  but it's lazy from a creative  perspective oh and speaking of lazy the  very best page in this chapter is page  12 aka the reveal of mastered ultra  instinct they're genuinely isn't much I  changed with this page beyond closing  the boxes because Torterra losses runoff  images but aside from that I wouldn't  change anything the images are clear  striking and expressive and wouldn't you  know it its composition is pretty much  entirely copied from the poses to the  expressions to the panel structure of  Akira Toriyama's Goku vs. piccolo jr.  fight look guys I understand there are  those out there that love Toyo taro and  Dragon Ball super smug and that's  perfectly fun more power to you as far  as I'm concerned Who am I to say what  you can enjoy and what you should enjoy  however if you are out there looking to  get into the industry and to start your  own comic  I implore you to not use toy or Tarot as  an example of what you think you should  be aiming for look at the past four  incredible manga cars like Osamu Tezuka  Genji ito  Yusuke Murata or even akira toriyama  there are tons of incredibly  Valentin monica's that have paved the  way and are continuing to pave the way  in some respects for young and  up-and-comers right now you are part of  a generation that has access to more  information and resources than any other  generation that has come before you I  truly believe that the greatest mangas  and comic book artists to date will  emerge in the next 20 years because of  this fact but that won't happen if we  act like visually uninteresting  composition full of noise  sloppy panel structure and suspect  referencing ethics are clogging our  perception of what makes a great or even  competent Monica and to all the aspiring  comic book and manga artists that this  video might reach do not give up doing  things the right way might seem  difficult but you have way more  potential than you give yourself credit  for you do not need to take shortcuts  work hard practice draw create innovate  improve change rice inspire repeat I  believe in you you are better than this  thank you so much for watching

